lass="Text"><span role="status" aria-live="polite">Rate this book</span></span></div></div></div></div><div data-testid="description" class="BookPageMetadataSection__description"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><div class="DetailsLayoutRightParagraph"><div class="DetailsLayoutRightParagraph__widthConstrained"><span class="Formatted">He doesn’t want to be king.<br />She doesn’t want to be a princess.<br />He doesn’t have a choice.<br />She does.<br /><br />Princes of New Sargasso<br />Book 1<br /><br />Prince Gideon of New Sargasso is used to people deferring to him.<br /><br />He’s even had supermodels offer to have his babies - quite a sacrifice for someone who makes their living in bikinis.<br /><br />So when he walks into a local Aussie-inspired café to find Karsen Robertson laughing to the point<br />of tears at the idea, he’s a little shocked.<br /><br />Then she makes him pay for his food.<br /><br />No one does that.<br /><br />But nothing and no one has intrigued him quite like the blue-eyed beauty who has nothing but<br />snark for him.<br /><br />Of course he’s going to ask her out.<br /><br />And, if he can keep the paparazzi and tabloids away long enough, finagle a way to make her a<br />princess.<br /><br />But if she’s not sure about the princess thing, how would she feel about one day becoming<br />queen?<br /><br />First dinner with a prince.<br /><br />Then a crown.<br /><br />If she doesn’t run screaming first.</span></div></div></div><div class=""></div></div></div><div data-testid="genresList" class="BookPageMetadataSection__genres"><ul class="CollapsableList" aria-label="Top genres for this book"><span tabindex="-1"><span class="BookPageMetadataSection__genrePlainText"><span class="Text Text__body3 Text__subdued">Genres</span></span><span class="BookPageMetadataSection__genreButton"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/genres/