 by Tamela Hancock Murray of The Steve Laube Agency.","isGrAuthor":true,"works":{"__typename":"ContributorWorksConnection","totalCount":79},"profileImageUrl":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/authors/1415569840i/9833345._UY200_CR49,0,200,200_.jpg","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/9833345.Carol_Moncado","viewerIsFollowing":null,"followers":{"__typename":"ContributorFollowersConnection","totalCount":387},"user":{"__ref":"User:11304509"}},"Series:kca://series/amzn1.gr.series.v3.UlqYDhy6LRcGZq-M":{"__typename":"Series","id":"kca://series/amzn1.gr.series.v3.UlqYDhy6LRcGZq-M","title":"The Princes of New Sargasso","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/series/311558-the-princes-of-new-sargasso"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.0FtN7jLXffzX56bc":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.0FtN7jLXffzX56bc","legacyId":54245589,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/54245589-dinner-with-a-prince","viewerShelving":null,"title":"Dinner with a Prince","titleComplete":"Dinner with a Prince  (The Princes of New Sargasso #1)","description":"He doesn’t want to be king.\u003cbr /\u003eShe doesn’t want to be a princess.\u003cbr /\u003eHe doesn’t have a choice.\u003cbr /\u003eShe does.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ePrinces of New Sargasso\u003cbr /\u003eBook 1\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ePrince Gideon of New Sargasso is used to people deferring to him.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHe’s even had supermodels offer to have his babies - quite a sacrifice for someone who makes their living in bikinis.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo when he walks into a local Aussie-inspired café to find Karsen Robertson laughing to the point\u003cbr /\u003eof tears at the idea, he’s a little shocked.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThen she makes him pay for his food.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNo one does that.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut nothing and no one has intrigued him quite like the blue-eyed beauty who has nothing but\u003cbr /\u003esnark for him.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOf course he’s going to ask her out.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd, if he can keep the paparazzi and tabloids away long enough, finagle a way to make her a\u003cbr /\u003eprincess.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut if she’s not sure about the princess thing, how would she feel about one day becoming\u003cbr /\u003equeen?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFirst dinner with a prince.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThen a crown.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIf she doesn’t run screaming first.","description({\"stripped\":true})":"He doesn’t want to be king.\r\nShe doesn’t want to be a princess.\r\nHe doesn’t have a choice.\r\nShe does.\r\n\r\nPrinces of New Sargasso\r\nBook 1\r\n\r\nPrince Gideon of New Sargasso is used to people deferring to him.\r\n\r\nHe’s even had supermodels offer to have his babies - quite a sacrifice for someone who makes their living in bikinis.\r\n\r\nSo when he walks into a local Aussie-inspired café to find Karsen Robertson laughing to the point\r\nof tears at the idea, he’s a little shocked.\r\n\r\nThen she makes him pay for his food.\r\n\r\nNo one does that.\r\n\r\nBut nothing and no one has intrigued him quite like the blue-eyed beauty who has nothing but\r\nsnark for him.\r\n\r\nOf course he’s going to ask her out.\r\n\r\nAnd, if he can keep the paparazzi and tabloids away long enough, finagle a way to make her a\r\nprincess.\r\n\r\nBut if she’s not sure about the princess thing, how would she feel about one day becoming\r\nqueen?\r\n\r\nFirst dinner with a prince.\r\n\r\nThen a crown.\r\n\r\nIf she doesn’t run screaming first.","primaryContributorEdge":{"__typename":"BookContributorEdge","node":{"__ref":"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.btXipjWzFEnRVhvImyMtVg"},"role":"Author"},"secondaryContributorEdges":[],"imageUrl":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1592969413i/54245589.jpg","bookSeries":[{"__typename":"BookSeries","us